VoiceLnq Desktop

This directory contains a modified version of Whispering 7.11.0,
Copyright (C) 2023-2025 Braden Wong,
from https://github.com/EpicenterHQ/epicenter (tag v7.11.0).

Modified by the VoiceLnq project, 2026. The changes began on 2026-11-16 and
include: renaming the app (VoiceFlow, then VoiceLnq from November 2026) with
new icons and a new application identifier, removing the Aptabase analytics,
disabling the upstream automatic updater, removing upstream's deployment scripts, new default OpenAI models for
transcription and tidy-up, storing API keys in the operating system's
credential store, pasting nothing when tidy-up fails (with Retry and Paste raw
text), an About screen, pointing links and model downloads away from
upstream, a new look, checking which app is being dictated into before
recording and again before pasting (privacy gates), keeping the app
running in the tray when its window is closed, with its own tray menu and a
hidden start at login, a floating recording bar (per-dictation style and
expression, voice feedback), dictation hotkeys handled natively
(the recorder starts in Rust even while the window sleeps) with every
webview created with WebView2 switches that keep it from being backgrounded,
keeping recordings as 16 kHz mono audio uploaded
as FLAC (split when very long), VoiceLnq's own version numbering (0.9.0),
and rebuilt Home, History, Styles, Settings and first-run screens with saved
spellings kept as local profile operations, and a language check after
tidy-up that keeps the speaker's own words when part of a mixed-language
dictation comes back translated, and the speaker's word list given to the
tidy-up so it can fix a misheard word from context. The full list of changes
is the git history of this directory since the commit "Import Whispering
7.11.0 into desktop/"; desktop/UPSTREAM.md says how to compare with upstream.

